<article class="env-lemma" id="0CW8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CW8">Lemma <span data-tag="0CW8">77.7.7</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/083F" data-tag="083F">77.7.1</a> suppose given an affine morphism $g : X \to X'$. Set $u' = f_*u : f_*\mathcal{F} \to f_*\mathcal{G}$. Then $F_{u, iso} = F_{u', iso}$, $F_{u, inj} = F_{u', inj}$, $F_{u, surj} = F_{u', surj}$, and $F_{u, zero} = F_{u', zero}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Cohomology of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07U8" data-tag="07U8">69.11.1</a> we have $g_{T, *}u_ T = u'_ T$. Moreover, $g_{T, *} : \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{X_ T}) \to \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is a faithful, exact functor reflecting isomorphisms, injective maps, and surjective maps. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>